~ start
Premier Bagnasco: You came in harvest week, Mr President, so everyone here is too tired to be anything but honest. Ask what you came to ask.
- Ask about the migration compact => migration
- Ask about the southern railway => railway
- Ask about the vintage => vintage
~ migration
Premier Bagnasco: Rome has carried that compact alone for a decade. We will talk about a compact when someone else's coast is as long as ours.
- Offer shared reception centres => centres
- Offer funding without centres => funding
~ centres
Premier Bagnasco: Centres in France as well? That would be a first. My interior minister will ask to see it in writing, twice.
=> END
~ funding
Premier Bagnasco: Money is welcome and does not fight the tide. But it is a start, and I have learned to take starts.
=> END
~ railway
Premier Bagnasco: The Messina bridge, the Salerno line, the one near Foggia that has been a promise since my grandfather. Pick one.
- Pledge French engineering for the Salerno line => salerno
- Pledge nothing, only interest => interest
~ salerno
Premier Bagnasco: Salerno. The south will hang your portrait in the station, next to the saint's.
=> END
~ interest
Premier Bagnasco: Interest is how the south has been paid for a hundred years. Still, your sincerity is noted.
=> END
~ vintage
Premier Bagnasco: A fair year. Not a great one, which is the kind that makes better wine than a great year makes politicians.
- Propose a wine and olive oil pact => pact
- Raise a glass and say nothing more => glass
~ pact
Premier Bagnasco: A pact on appellations. Between us we make half the wine on earth, and we have never agreed on what it is called.
=> END
~ glass
Premier Bagnasco: To the harvest. Politics will still be there on Monday, regrettably.
=> END
